# (1486) Marilyn from ALCDEF light curves

Script: [`examples/1486_marilyn_alcdef.jl`](https://github.com/mkretlow/Lightcurves.jl/blob/main/examples/1486_marilyn_alcdef.jl).

Five dense light curves of 2013 are downloaded from alcdef.org ([`fetch_alcdef`](@ref)) and compared with the LCDB entry
([`lcdb_entry`](@ref)). The times are corrected for light time with the geocentric distance from JPL Horizons
([`observing_geometry`](@ref), [`light_time_correct`](@ref)). FALC with one zero point per session finds the rotation
period, the GLS periodogram half of it (double-peaked light curve); [`fit_period`](@ref) refines the period with its
error, and the result is plotted in the style of the Minor Planet Bulletin (`plot(fit; residuals=true)`).

!!! note "Output"
    The script is not run when the manual is built; output and figures of its last run:

```text
{{OUTPUT}}
